{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1780500684,"nonce":"fFmq4gf/Bhe7gt8QM4u4Ylq5ubE=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABERD9fw","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/214","origin":"github"},"title":"BizzyBoat CTD winch not working — device does not enumerate on gabby","message":"## Summary\n\nBizzyBoat's CTD (SmartCast) winch is not working. When attempting to operate it\nvia the RC controller, the winch does not respond, and the winch device **does\nnot show up on gabby**. A boat power cycle did **not** resolve it.\n\n## Symptoms\n\n- Winch does not actuate when commanded from the RC controller.\n- The winch serial device is **absent on gabby** (no `/dev/winch`, and presumably\n  no underlying `/dev/ttyACM*` for the Arduino).\n- **Power-cycling the boat did not fix it.**\n\n## Device details (for diagnosis)\n\nThe CTD winch is driven by an Arduino controller that is part of the factory\nSmartCast system:\n\n| Item | Value |\n|------|-------|\n| Device | Arduino CTD winch controller (SmartCast) |\n| udev symlink | `/dev/winch` |\n| VID:PID | `2341:0043` |\n| Serial | `342343139313512040B1` |\n| Typical node | `/dev/ttyACM2` |\n\nudev rule + ModemManager exclusion were set up under #26\n(`docs/bizzyboat_udev_setup_2026-03-31.md`).\n\n## Prior history\n\nThe udev setup notes (2026-03-31) record that this Arduino has **failed to\nenumerate before** and only **\"came back after a firm re-seat\"** of the USB\nconnection. So intermittent USB enumeration on this device has precedent — a\nloose/failed cable or connector is a leading suspect.\n\n## Suggested diagnostics (gabby)\n\n- [ ] `lsusb | grep -i 2341` — is the Arduino enumerating on USB at all?\n- [ ] `ls -l /dev/ttyACM* /dev/winch` and `dmesg | tail -50` after re-plug —\n      kernel see the device?\n- [ ] Firm re-seat / swap the USB cable and the Arduino's USB port (per the\n      2026-03-31 re-seat fix).\n- [ ] Check winch power rail / Arduino power LED (distinguish dead board vs USB).\n- [ ] If it enumerates but won't drive: check ModemManager isn't grabbing it,\n      and verify the RC → winch command path.\n\n## Context / urgency\n\nThis is **pre-class** (Summer Hydro). The hydro payload install log already flags\nan open TODO to *bench-test the SmartCast winch end-to-end before the class*\n(`bizzyboat_project11/docs/hydro_payload_install_log.md`), so this needs to be\nresolved before survey ops. Related: hydro payload integration #76.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`\n**Reported by**: Roland (field test attempt)","files":null}]}